gh  definition camera footage um and  that's all we've done we've mapped it  we've it can now be protected and  respected and studied in the future  who knows in decades time they may have  the technology to reach down raise it up  and preserve it somewhere for all of  humankind but that's a long way off but  certainly no plans do anything with it  in the in the near term  right and and what does this mean for  other shipwrecks around the world  well i think what it means is it  hopefully will add rocket fuel to  people's fascination with what lies  about our oceans there are there's  probably more heritage more treasures on  our ocean floor than there are all the  museums of the world combined so we do  have the technology now to see down to  those wrecks we and we have a duty to  protect them because there are people  out there bad actors who want to sell  who want to you know loot and and  desecrate those wrecks so i think for  people like me we'd love to get down  there get data on the wrecks broadcast  into the world help people i mean i  don't need much help  falling in love with history i've got to  say but for some people i can understand  they need a little bit of they need to  see something and to feel something and  i think when you broadcast these images  and these laser 3d models i think it  will just engage a whole generation in  not just for shackleton and antarctic  but with subsidy adventure in its  entirety  dan snow in antarctica thanks very much  indeed great to have your enthusiasm as  part of the program today thank you

